`verilator_config
// PINMISSING is an ERROR in this flow (see CMakeLists.txt), because an
// unconnected INPUT is otherwise silent in everything the workspace runs:
// iverilog has no missing-pin diagnostic at all, and a plain warning would not
// fail a build that also passes -Wno-fatal. That silence cost a month once --
// hh-c128's machine tops never connected z180_mem_subsys.wstrb_i and the
// machines took NO RAM WRITES AT ALL (hh-c128 PROGRESS 6.27).
//
// A TESTBENCH is the one place where leaving pins off is legitimate: it
// instantiates the DUT to exercise one thing and ignores the outputs it does
// not score. So the rule keeps its teeth on every RTL-to-RTL instantiation --
// which is where the defect class lives -- and is waived for bench files only.
//
// Deliberately unused pins in RTL should be written `.pin()`, explicitly empty:
// that says "unused on purpose" where omission says nothing.
lint_off -rule PINMISSING -file "*tb_*.sv"
